Development Meeting Summary
Date: 9th Feb 2026
Location / Platform: Online
1. Focus of This Week
The main goal for this week is to connect the entire system into a runnable prototype, moving from isolated components to an end-to-end workflow.
The priority is integration over optimisation.
2. Backend–IR Communication (REST API)
Objective
Enable communication between the backend and the IR system via a REST API.
Key Points
The IR system (indexing, querying, ranking) will be exposed through API endpoints.
The backend acts as the coordinator:
Receives requests from the frontend
Calls the IR components
Fetches metadata from the database
Returns results in JSON format
Outcome
A minimal but functional API layer that allows queries to reach the IR system.
3. End-to-End Data Flow (Frontend → IR → Database)
Target Pipeline
Frontend → REST API → IR System → Database → Results → Frontend
Responsibilities
Frontend:
Collect user queries (boolean / free-text)
Send requests to the backend API
Backend / IR:
Parse queries
Execute retrieval on the index
Fetch document metadata from the database
Database:
Store headlines, URLs, timestamps, and other metadata
Support fast lookup during result construction
Goal
Ensure the full pipeline runs correctly for basic search queries.
4. Deployment Considerations (Cloud)
Objective
Prepare the system to be runnable in a cloud environment.
Scope (Prototype Level)
Push the backend + IR system to the cloud.
Ensure:
API endpoints remain accessible
The system can run outside local machines
Note
This step focuses on deployability, not scalability or performance tuning.
5. Documentation and Report Draft
Tasks
Start drafting the project report alongside implementation.
Clearly document:
System architecture
Data flow
API design
Current limitations
API Documentation
Define API endpoints clearly (inputs, outputs).
Keep API design consistent with system architecture described in the report.
6. Relation to Previous Decisions
This week’s tasks build directly on earlier meetings:
RSS-based crawling and time-based storage are assumed to be stable.
IR components (boolean and free-text search) are now being integrated rather than developed in isolation.
Frontend design focuses on functionality first, UI refinement later.
7. Guiding Principle for This Week
Get the full system running first, then iterate and optimise.
A working prototype is the highest priority; feature completeness and performance improvements can follow once the system is stable.
